WEBVTT

00:00:13.140 --> 00:00:16.230
I played some games with Kouta and Mitsuki yesterday.

00:00:17.740 --> 00:00:19.730
I couldn't beat them at all.

00:00:20.070 --> 00:00:21.230
Onee-chan!

00:00:21.480 --> 00:00:22.230
What?

00:00:23.150 --> 00:00:25.150
Were you calling me?

00:00:25.650 --> 00:00:27.780
Oh... S-Sorry, it was a mistake...

00:00:28.270 --> 00:00:30.830
Like calling your teacher "Mum"?

00:00:32.240 --> 00:00:34.490
I'm so embarrassed!

00:00:34.490 --> 00:00:36.620
Mum!

00:00:37.000 --> 00:00:38.120
Shino!

00:00:38.120 --> 00:00:39.580
Calm down!

00:02:17.140 --> 00:02:20.390
Everyone's done that at least once or twice.

00:02:20.390 --> 00:02:23.400
Youko and Shinobu seem like sisters sometimes.

00:02:23.980 --> 00:02:26.020
We've known each other a long time.

00:02:26.020 --> 00:02:27.320
Really?

00:02:27.320 --> 00:02:31.780
Shino and I have been friends since elementary school.

00:02:31.780 --> 00:02:33.780
Not long after we started school...

00:02:35.030 --> 00:02:36.990
A yoghurt.

00:02:36.990 --> 00:02:38.700
I had a yoghurt, too.

00:02:38.700 --> 00:02:40.080
What kind of yoghurt?

00:02:40.080 --> 00:02:41.290
A kiwi yoghurt.

00:02:41.600 --> 00:02:43.500
Me, too!

00:02:43.500 --> 00:02:44.790
Kiwis are so cool, aren't they?

00:02:44.790 --> 00:02:46.470
Really cool.

00:02:47.300 --> 00:02:49.090
Shinobu-chan, what are you doing?

00:02:50.090 --> 00:02:52.510
I'm looking for my sister.

00:02:52.510 --> 00:02:54.550
You won't find her in there.

00:02:57.470 --> 00:02:59.310
You were lost?

00:02:59.310 --> 00:03:01.260
You sure are hopeless, aren't you?

00:03:02.100 --> 00:03:04.850
This is my sister's class.

00:03:05.810 --> 00:03:08.980
Oh, you brought Shinobu here?

00:03:09.320 --> 00:03:11.150
You're... Youko-chan, right?

00:03:11.530 --> 00:03:12.860
While she's at school,

00:03:12.860 --> 00:03:15.030
could you look after my sister for me?

00:03:15.030 --> 00:03:15.780
Huh?

00:03:16.240 --> 00:03:20.290
She's a bit absent-minded, so I worry that she'll get into trouble.

00:03:20.290 --> 00:03:21.490
I know!

00:03:21.490 --> 00:03:24.430
If anything happens, use this.

00:03:25.370 --> 00:03:27.130
I'll come running.

00:03:27.130 --> 00:03:29.050
That's not what that's for!

00:03:33.840 --> 00:03:36.090
<i>She is pretty absent-minded.</i>

00:03:36.090 --> 00:03:38.050
<i>She seems like the type who'd get kidnapped.</i>

00:03:38.050 --> 00:03:41.060
Youko-chan, you're just like a big sister.

00:03:41.800 --> 00:03:44.940
<i>I need to protect her in place of her sister.</i>

00:03:49.770 --> 00:03:50.860
<i>We're being followed.</i>

00:03:52.400 --> 00:03:55.260
<i>This</i> the right way to use a personal alarm!

00:03:56.110 --> 00:03:57.200
What's going on here?

00:03:57.200 --> 00:03:58.320
Onee-san!

00:03:59.080 --> 00:04:01.580
And that's how we got to be what we are now.

00:04:01.580 --> 00:04:05.370
I feel like that turned into a story about Isa-nee somewhere along the way...

00:04:06.540 --> 00:04:08.190
I see.

00:04:08.190 --> 00:04:09.460
Youko, you definitely do...

00:04:10.920 --> 00:04:12.210
Um...

00:04:12.210 --> 00:04:13.380
Act like an older sister?

00:04:13.380 --> 00:04:14.800
Yes, exactly!

00:04:15.720 --> 00:04:17.860
Ayaya, you...

00:04:17.860 --> 00:04:18.640
What?

00:04:19.850 --> 00:04:21.100
You act like an Ayaya.

00:04:21.100 --> 00:04:22.850
What does that mean?!

00:04:26.060 --> 00:04:27.600
Aya-chan.

00:04:27.910 --> 00:04:29.940
Will you help me study?

00:04:29.940 --> 00:04:31.130
Sure.

00:04:31.130 --> 00:04:33.360
How did your last test go, Shino?

00:04:33.710 --> 00:04:37.500
Not very well...

00:04:37.500 --> 00:04:38.620
You got a zero?

00:04:38.950 --> 00:04:41.390
You call that "not very well"?

00:04:41.390 --> 00:04:43.950
You couldn't have scored any lower.

00:04:44.450 --> 00:04:46.870
This score's unbelievaball.

00:04:47.460 --> 00:04:48.330
A ball?

00:04:48.710 --> 00:04:50.200
Nevermind.

00:04:50.200 --> 00:04:51.800
Here, sit down.

00:04:53.170 --> 00:04:54.590
There's a make-up test,

00:04:54.590 --> 00:04:57.260
so just remember what I teach you and you'll be fine.

00:04:57.260 --> 00:04:58.550
Let's get to work.

00:04:58.550 --> 00:04:59.740
Yes, a ball.

00:04:59.740 --> 00:05:01.970
X equals five here...

00:05:01.970 --> 00:05:03.130
Yes, a ball.

00:05:03.130 --> 00:05:05.350
Calculate this first, and...

00:05:05.350 --> 00:05:06.940
Yes, a ball.

00:05:06.940 --> 00:05:08.850
I solved it, a ball.

00:05:08.850 --> 00:05:09.850
Oh, come on!

00:05:09.850 --> 00:05:11.360
I didn't mean to say it that way!

00:05:11.360 --> 00:05:13.480
You don't have to keep repeating it!

00:05:13.480 --> 00:05:14.080
What?

00:05:14.080 --> 00:05:15.820
I thought it was going to be on the test...

00:05:15.820 --> 00:05:18.610
You don't need to remember that.

00:05:18.610 --> 00:05:21.200
Will you teach me, too?

00:05:21.870 --> 00:05:23.540
Oh, sure.

00:05:24.330 --> 00:05:25.580
Me, too.

00:05:25.580 --> 00:05:27.410
Teach me as well, please.

00:05:28.500 --> 00:05:31.670
In that case, why don't we have a study party?

00:05:36.510 --> 00:05:38.590
I'm kinda nervous.

00:05:38.590 --> 00:05:41.520
Is this your first time meeting Isa-nee?

00:05:41.520 --> 00:05:44.010
I've seen her plenty of times in magazines.

00:05:44.010 --> 00:05:44.940
Really?

00:05:44.940 --> 00:05:47.480
I don't look at fashion magazines much.

00:05:47.480 --> 00:05:51.860
Yes, as a hugely popular high school fashion model,

00:05:51.860 --> 00:05:54.610
many girls admire Isami!

00:05:54.610 --> 00:05:57.240
How many autographs will she give me?

00:05:57.240 --> 00:06:00.070
You only came to Japan recently, didn't you?

00:06:01.160 --> 00:06:03.200
Excuse the intrusion.

00:06:03.490 --> 00:06:04.880
Welcome.

00:06:04.880 --> 00:06:06.700
What brings you all here today?

00:06:06.700 --> 00:06:08.330
Hey, Isa-nee.

00:06:08.330 --> 00:06:10.890
We're here to study.

00:06:11.580 --> 00:06:14.380
Um, this is for everyone in the house to share.

00:06:14.380 --> 00:06:15.200
How nice of you.

00:06:15.200 --> 00:06:16.710
Thank you.

00:06:16.710 --> 00:06:18.340
My name is Kujou Karen.

00:06:18.920 --> 00:06:23.050
I became a fan of yours after seeing you in a magazine.

00:06:23.050 --> 00:06:26.470
If you don't mind, I was hoping to get your autograph.

00:06:26.760 --> 00:06:29.350
Karen's Japanese just got fluent!

00:06:29.350 --> 00:06:30.640
Why?

00:06:38.400 --> 00:06:40.030
Aya-chan, this problem...

00:06:40.030 --> 00:06:42.910
For this one, use this equation.

00:06:44.740 --> 00:06:48.080
Onee-chan, will you show me how to do this?

00:06:48.080 --> 00:06:50.660
Sure, but it'll cost you.

00:06:50.660 --> 00:06:52.040
You want money?

00:06:52.040 --> 00:06:54.290
Give me one of your treasured possessions or something.

00:06:56.040 --> 00:06:57.980
Very well.

00:06:57.980 --> 00:06:59.130
In that case...

00:07:01.130 --> 00:07:04.930
I'll give you one of my most treasured possessions: a Venetian mask!

00:07:04.930 --> 00:07:06.220
I don't want that thing.

00:07:07.260 --> 00:07:10.220
You call my treasure "that thing"?!

00:07:16.690 --> 00:07:18.230
It's almost lunchtime.

00:07:21.950 --> 00:07:24.710
Aya, did your stomach just growl?

00:07:24.710 --> 00:07:25.970
It wasn't me.

00:07:25.970 --> 00:07:27.120
It must have been you.

00:07:27.120 --> 00:07:27.540
What?

00:07:27.540 --> 00:07:28.700
No.

00:07:28.700 --> 00:07:30.050
Then, it must have been Alice!

00:07:30.050 --> 00:07:31.500
It was you, wasn't it?

00:07:31.500 --> 00:07:34.000
I-It wasn't me.

00:07:35.200 --> 00:07:35.870
I'm sorry!

00:07:35.870 --> 00:07:36.500
I lied!

00:07:36.500 --> 00:07:38.920
It was my stomach that growled!

00:07:39.920 --> 00:07:42.720
Aya-chan made us lunch.

00:07:43.430 --> 00:07:44.880
Amazing.

00:07:44.880 --> 00:07:46.390
You made all this yourself?

00:07:46.390 --> 00:07:47.760
You're such a good cook.

00:07:47.760 --> 00:07:48.550
What?

00:07:48.550 --> 00:07:51.020
You'll make a good wife, Aya.

00:07:51.020 --> 00:07:52.850
No, I...

00:07:52.850 --> 00:07:55.520
That's not true, silly!

00:07:55.520 --> 00:07:57.230
That smile looks so happy!

00:07:57.610 --> 00:07:59.150
Let's eat.

00:08:02.030 --> 00:08:05.030
<i>It looks perfect, but the flavour's not quite there.</i>

00:08:05.030 --> 00:08:06.530
<i>In fact, there's barely any flavour.</i>

00:08:06.910 --> 00:08:10.280
<i>But that smile... I can't say anything that might hurt her.</i>

00:08:10.280 --> 00:08:10.950
How is it?

00:08:11.370 --> 00:08:12.500
Um, it's good...

00:08:12.500 --> 00:08:14.660
It doesn't have much flavour.

00:08:14.660 --> 00:08:17.420
Can't you be a bit more sensitive?!

00:08:18.040 --> 00:08:20.000
Thanks for the food.

00:08:23.750 --> 00:08:26.800
Aya-chan, I bet you'd look great in Japanese clothing.

00:08:29.760 --> 00:08:32.350
You mean these clothes don't suit me?

00:08:32.680 --> 00:08:34.350
Of course they do.

00:08:34.350 --> 00:08:37.600
I think your choice of outfit looks great on you.

00:08:38.600 --> 00:08:42.320
The most important thing is to wear clothes that look good on you.

00:08:44.870 --> 00:08:46.070
You're blushing!

00:08:53.620 --> 00:08:55.370
Excuse the intrusion.

00:09:02.300 --> 00:09:04.660
What a cool camera.

00:09:04.660 --> 00:09:06.570
Karen-chan?

00:09:06.570 --> 00:09:08.840
What are you doing in my room?

00:09:08.840 --> 00:09:11.470
I-I'm sorry for entering without your permission!

00:09:11.470 --> 00:09:13.320
It's okay...

00:09:14.730 --> 00:09:15.600
No!

00:09:15.600 --> 00:09:16.650
Not the police!

00:09:16.650 --> 00:09:19.270
Anything but the police!

00:09:19.270 --> 00:09:21.360
It's my friend calling.

00:09:22.480 --> 00:09:24.650
I don't mind having my picture taken,

00:09:24.650 --> 00:09:26.190
but I like taking pictures even more.

00:09:26.940 --> 00:09:29.180
Will someone pose for me?

00:09:30.320 --> 00:09:32.120
Okay, Aya-chan, pose.

00:09:32.120 --> 00:09:33.330
What, me?

00:09:33.740 --> 00:09:35.870
U-Um...

00:09:37.830 --> 00:09:38.750
Huh?

00:09:40.120 --> 00:09:44.130
Um... Can you take pictures of me as if I'm a model?

00:09:44.440 --> 00:09:45.660
Sure.

00:09:45.660 --> 00:09:46.920
But instead of taking them here,

00:09:46.920 --> 00:09:49.130
why don't we go to the park nearby?

00:09:52.890 --> 00:09:54.720
This place brings back memories.

00:09:54.720 --> 00:09:58.680
I used to play here with Onee-chan when we were little.

00:09:58.680 --> 00:09:59.890
Really?

00:10:07.990 --> 00:10:11.050
You've grown so much, Shinobu.

00:10:11.050 --> 00:10:13.410
Where did that come from?

00:10:14.080 --> 00:10:16.240
Are you ready?

00:10:16.240 --> 00:10:17.290
Yes.

00:10:17.790 --> 00:10:21.040
<i>It's time to show the results of my daily practising in front of the mirror!</i>

00:10:23.630 --> 00:10:25.340
Try to make your poses more natural.

00:10:25.340 --> 00:10:26.580
<i>No way!</i>

00:10:27.590 --> 00:10:30.090
Isa-nee, let's take one together.

00:10:30.090 --> 00:10:31.180
Okay.

00:10:31.630 --> 00:10:33.770
Shinobu, will you take the picture?

00:10:33.770 --> 00:10:34.430
Sure.

00:10:35.680 --> 00:10:37.010
Are you ready?

00:10:37.010 --> 00:10:38.430
Wait a second.

00:10:39.230 --> 00:10:40.440
I'm embarrassed to stand next to a model.

00:10:40.440 --> 00:10:43.150
It makes my face look bigger.

00:10:43.150 --> 00:10:45.230
Let's stand a little farther back.

00:10:45.940 --> 00:10:47.440
I'm taking the picture now.

00:10:47.720 --> 00:10:49.360
Okay.

00:10:49.360 --> 00:10:50.490
Hey now...

00:10:52.030 --> 00:10:54.160
Thank you for today.

00:10:54.820 --> 00:10:57.200
I'll give Shinobu the photos when they've been developed.

00:10:57.620 --> 00:10:58.760
If you don't mind,

00:10:58.760 --> 00:11:03.250
can you please show them to a model photographer?

00:11:03.250 --> 00:11:06.880
Isami, please put in a good word for us.

00:11:08.210 --> 00:11:09.460
We'll see...

00:11:09.460 --> 00:11:10.840
Isami!

00:11:10.840 --> 00:11:11.840
You two...

00:11:18.260 --> 00:11:21.810
This is the English girl staying at your house?

00:11:21.810 --> 00:11:22.810
Yeah.

00:11:22.810 --> 00:11:26.150
I know she speaks Japanese, but what's it like living with her?

00:11:26.150 --> 00:11:27.150
Have you got used to it?

00:11:30.990 --> 00:11:34.280
It's like having two really cute little sisters.

00:11:34.280 --> 00:11:36.950
You really do have a sister complex, don't you?

00:11:43.710 --> 00:11:45.250
<i>When we were little,</i>

00:11:45.250 --> 00:11:47.880
<i>Shinobu was an absent-minded child,</i>

00:11:47.880 --> 00:11:50.800
<i>and I was always worried about her...</i>

00:11:51.320 --> 00:11:52.550
<i>But recently,</i>

00:11:52.550 --> 00:11:55.180
<i>maybe because she found something she's passionate about,</i>

00:11:55.180 --> 00:11:58.350
<i>she seems to have it together a little more than she used to.</i>

00:11:59.560 --> 00:12:01.270
Wear this one next.

00:12:01.810 --> 00:12:03.810
And put on this dress after that.

00:12:03.810 --> 00:12:04.520
Come on.

00:12:07.520 --> 00:12:10.650
<i>I'm a little worried about my sister's future.</i>

00:12:12.030 --> 00:12:13.030
Come on.

00:12:28.130 --> 00:12:30.290
Youko, I'm sure this comes a bit late,

00:12:30.290 --> 00:12:31.710
but you should wear your uniform properly.

00:12:32.090 --> 00:12:34.340
That really did come late...

00:12:34.340 --> 00:12:36.630
I wear it properly at ceremonies.

00:12:36.970 --> 00:12:39.800
You should dress properly all the time.

00:12:40.210 --> 00:12:43.020
The buttons are choking me.

00:12:43.560 --> 00:12:45.860
<i>T-This is kind of like...</i>

00:12:47.650 --> 00:12:50.020
Why are you blushing?

00:12:52.940 --> 00:12:53.900
Well?

00:12:54.230 --> 00:12:55.530
It looks nice.

00:12:55.530 --> 00:12:58.110
I haven't seen you like this since the entrance ceremony.

00:12:58.110 --> 00:13:00.120
You look very mature.

00:13:00.620 --> 00:13:02.490
How do I usually look?

00:13:03.080 --> 00:13:05.200
Youko, we want to ask you something.

00:13:06.120 --> 00:13:06.790
What?

00:13:07.070 --> 00:13:09.000
Hey, where's Youko?

00:13:09.000 --> 00:13:10.630
Where is Youko?

00:13:10.920 --> 00:13:12.090
Youko?

00:13:12.090 --> 00:13:13.550
Where are you?

00:13:14.010 --> 00:13:14.740
Where is she?

00:13:14.740 --> 00:13:15.010
You can't be serious!

00:13:15.010 --> 00:13:16.420
Youko?
You can't be serious!

00:13:20.800 --> 00:13:23.770
Youko, let's arm wrestle.

00:13:23.770 --> 00:13:24.930
Arm wrestle you?

00:13:26.350 --> 00:13:28.690
Ready... go!

00:13:36.070 --> 00:13:37.190
There!

00:13:38.360 --> 00:13:39.320
I won...

00:13:40.240 --> 00:13:41.410
I won!

00:13:41.870 --> 00:13:42.950
Aw.

00:13:42.950 --> 00:13:43.990
I lost.

00:13:47.540 --> 00:13:50.000
Now I could take on a bear!

00:13:50.370 --> 00:13:53.630
I'm not a bear, you know!

00:13:54.460 --> 00:13:55.800
Like this?

00:13:55.800 --> 00:13:57.420
What is that stance?

00:14:07.220 --> 00:14:08.640
Are you okay, Karen?

00:14:09.190 --> 00:14:10.230
Youko.

00:14:10.770 --> 00:14:12.410
Are you taking those to your classroom?

00:14:12.410 --> 00:14:13.480
I'll help you.

00:14:14.150 --> 00:14:15.670
Thank you.

00:14:15.670 --> 00:14:17.070
That helps a lot.

00:14:18.900 --> 00:14:20.820
Okay, let's go.

00:14:21.450 --> 00:14:22.320
Hey...

00:14:22.580 --> 00:14:23.740
Thank you.

00:14:24.280 --> 00:14:27.120
You're always there to lend a hand when I need it.

00:14:27.120 --> 00:14:29.370
Everyone should have a friend like you.

00:14:29.370 --> 00:14:30.620
Well, thanks.

00:14:31.330 --> 00:14:33.580
You're always standing around quietly and smiling,

00:14:33.580 --> 00:14:36.500
but you're listening to everything we have to say.

00:14:36.500 --> 00:14:40.220
I'd feel reassured if I met you on the street at night.

00:14:40.220 --> 00:14:43.970
Yes, you're just like a convenience store!

00:14:44.550 --> 00:14:46.510
That's not a compliment.

00:14:50.720 --> 00:14:53.100
Shino, what's that mountain of paper?

00:14:53.980 --> 00:14:56.320
Fliers for overseas trips.

00:14:56.320 --> 00:15:01.610
My sister almost threw them away yesterday.

00:15:02.410 --> 00:15:05.160
They may look like ordinary pieces of paper,

00:15:05.160 --> 00:15:07.620
but they're my treasure.

00:15:07.620 --> 00:15:09.540
Fold, fold.

00:15:17.170 --> 00:15:19.050
Aya, are you feeling ill?

00:15:19.510 --> 00:15:21.010
I have a bit of a cold.

00:15:21.380 --> 00:15:22.390
Are you okay?

00:15:22.390 --> 00:15:23.300
Do you have a fever?

00:15:25.220 --> 00:15:27.810
W-What if my fever rises?!

00:15:28.140 --> 00:15:29.810
What?!

00:15:31.730 --> 00:15:32.310
Here.

00:15:32.660 --> 00:15:34.190
Wear a mask.

00:15:34.520 --> 00:15:36.190
Thanks.

00:15:42.150 --> 00:15:43.990
One pork bun, please.

00:15:44.320 --> 00:15:46.490
Drop the convenience store thing.

00:15:49.290 --> 00:15:52.290
I wonder what everyone thinks of me...

00:15:52.290 --> 00:15:54.500
I have no idea.

00:15:54.500 --> 00:15:57.170
Let's try expressing it using a pie chart.

00:15:57.500 --> 00:15:58.920
Like this one.

00:16:00.560 --> 00:16:04.220
Youko-chan, your pie chart...

00:16:09.760 --> 00:16:11.060
looks like this.

00:16:11.560 --> 00:16:13.600
Just what am I?!

00:16:27.510 --> 00:16:28.160
Hey!

00:16:28.160 --> 00:16:29.510
What are you writing?

00:16:29.510 --> 00:16:31.210
The curiosity's killing me!

00:16:32.830 --> 00:16:34.910
I'm making a revised Youko pie chart.

00:16:35.620 --> 00:16:40.170
After observing you today, I realised that this graph was incorrect.

00:16:40.590 --> 00:16:43.880
In other words, I'm not just here to make retorts?

00:16:44.340 --> 00:16:45.760
That is why I've made this revised version.

00:16:46.130 --> 00:16:48.140
And this is the chart Shino made.

00:16:49.050 --> 00:16:51.010
Do you see the difference?

00:16:52.960 --> 00:16:53.850
Stop!

00:16:53.850 --> 00:16:54.930
Everyone's looking!

00:16:58.190 --> 00:17:02.270
As you can see, half of you is made up of kindness.

00:17:04.110 --> 00:17:05.870
Oh, come on.

00:17:05.870 --> 00:17:07.380
You're embarrassing me.

00:17:08.990 --> 00:17:11.740
<i>But the other half is still comedic retorts.</i>

00:17:12.280 --> 00:17:15.580
By the way, I made an Ayaya pie chart, too.

00:17:15.580 --> 00:17:16.750
For me?

00:17:18.500 --> 00:17:21.460
What does the largest section represent?

00:17:21.810 --> 00:17:23.300
Youko, of course.

00:17:26.880 --> 00:17:28.250
Aya's pie chart?

00:17:28.250 --> 00:17:29.390
Let me see.

00:17:29.930 --> 00:17:35.020
I-It may not be 0%, but it's 5% at the most!

00:17:36.310 --> 00:17:37.310
What are you talking about?

00:17:37.780 --> 00:17:40.600
Are you sure you don't have a fever, Aya?

00:17:40.600 --> 00:17:42.570
I don't have a fever at all.

00:17:42.940 --> 00:17:44.570
Don't get the wrong idea.

00:17:45.190 --> 00:17:52.030
Youko-chan <i>does</i> seem nice, like an older sister or a mother.

00:17:52.450 --> 00:17:55.240
I don't remember becoming your mum, Shino.

00:17:55.670 --> 00:17:57.200
Now that you mention it,

00:17:57.200 --> 00:18:01.130
Shino accidentally called Youko "Onee-chan" the other day.

00:18:01.420 --> 00:18:03.750
Youko does seem like an older sister.

00:18:03.750 --> 00:18:04.880
You think so?

00:18:04.880 --> 00:18:06.960
I'm an only child.

00:18:06.960 --> 00:18:08.880
I wish I had an older sister.

00:18:09.760 --> 00:18:11.590
I'm an only child, too.

00:18:11.590 --> 00:18:13.260
So am I.

00:18:13.260 --> 00:18:15.850
I wish I had an older sister like you, Youko.

00:18:16.470 --> 00:18:18.060
That kinda makes me happy.

00:18:18.640 --> 00:18:20.520
Youko Onee-chan.

00:18:21.150 --> 00:18:23.400
What is it, little sis?

00:18:25.360 --> 00:18:27.030
O-Onee-chan...

00:18:28.030 --> 00:18:30.030
Stare...

00:18:33.280 --> 00:18:34.740
I have a question.

00:18:34.740 --> 00:18:36.790
Do you have any siblings, Sensei?

00:18:37.490 --> 00:18:40.250
I-I'm the youngest of three.

00:18:40.830 --> 00:18:43.250
I have two Onii-chans...

00:18:43.250 --> 00:18:46.750
Onii-chan?

00:18:50.550 --> 00:18:52.590
I-I mean, two older brothers.

00:18:52.590 --> 00:18:54.390
Let's get back to the lesson.

00:18:59.270 --> 00:19:01.390
Shino, are you going to the faculty office?

00:19:01.710 --> 00:19:02.980
Yes.

00:19:02.980 --> 00:19:05.810
You don't get lost around school anymore, huh?

00:19:05.810 --> 00:19:08.900
I'm not in elementary school.

00:19:08.900 --> 00:19:11.240
You don't need to hold my hand.

00:19:11.240 --> 00:19:13.230
I'm okay by myself.

00:19:17.830 --> 00:19:18.910
Is something wrong?

00:19:19.660 --> 00:19:22.670
I just started feeling a little sad.

00:19:23.580 --> 00:19:25.170
Since we started high school,

00:19:25.170 --> 00:19:26.960
and especially since Alice and Karen showed up,

00:19:26.960 --> 00:19:29.170
it feels like Shino's changed.

00:19:29.670 --> 00:19:31.300
When the three of them are together,

00:19:31.300 --> 00:19:33.680
Shino looks like their older sister.

00:19:40.720 --> 00:19:43.190
She looks like a captured space alien to me.

00:19:43.190 --> 00:19:44.560
You're ruining my moment!

00:19:45.150 --> 00:19:46.810
You don't have to worry about her.

00:19:46.810 --> 00:19:49.760
Shino can manage on her own.

00:19:49.760 --> 00:19:51.860
I agree.

00:19:51.860 --> 00:19:52.900
Me, too.

00:19:54.820 --> 00:19:56.660
For example, if she were abandoned in the middle of a desert,

00:19:56.660 --> 00:19:58.160
Such strong wind...

00:19:58.160 --> 00:20:00.240
she seems as if she'd come back home like nothing happened.

00:20:00.830 --> 00:20:02.500
If she were stranded on an uninhabited island,

00:20:02.500 --> 00:20:05.120
she seems like she could live well.

00:20:05.500 --> 00:20:07.840
If she got lost on Mount Everest...

00:20:07.840 --> 00:20:10.590
What kind of person do you think Shino is?!

00:20:11.210 --> 00:20:15.090
I know you view Shino as your little sister.

00:20:15.630 --> 00:20:18.550
It's been that way since elementary school.

00:20:19.260 --> 00:20:24.380
But since I'm the oldest child, I wish I had an older sister.

00:20:24.380 --> 00:20:27.270
Not that I don't like my younger siblings, though.

00:20:27.890 --> 00:20:31.360
Youko, you call Isami "Isa-nee".

00:20:31.820 --> 00:20:33.780
Yeah, guess I do.

00:20:34.900 --> 00:20:37.700
Youko-chan, you're like a little sister to me.

00:20:37.700 --> 00:20:38.410
Really?

00:20:38.410 --> 00:20:39.780
Yes, I like you a lot.

00:20:42.040 --> 00:20:46.000
Then, is it all right if I call you Isa-nee?

00:20:46.000 --> 00:20:46.960
Of course.

00:20:49.880 --> 00:20:51.460
Isa-nee.

00:20:54.970 --> 00:20:56.510
What time is it?

00:20:56.510 --> 00:20:58.090
It's...

00:21:01.720 --> 00:21:03.520
12:55.

00:21:04.600 --> 00:21:06.980
Has your sister complex escalated?

00:21:08.020 --> 00:21:09.560
You think so?

00:22:49.910 --> 00:22:53.420
My sister was scouted to become a model.

00:22:53.420 --> 00:22:54.590
That's amazing.

00:22:56.000 --> 00:22:59.210
She was scouted right around here.

00:22:59.720 --> 00:23:03.300
Maybe we'll be scouted, too.

00:23:03.930 --> 00:23:06.430
We're just waiting to be scouted, huh?

00:23:16.480 --> 00:23:19.530
I thought you two had gone home already.

00:23:21.430 --> 00:23:23.680
Onee-chan, how about this outfit?

00:23:23.680 --> 00:23:26.390
I think something else would suit you better.

00:23:26.390 --> 00:23:27.770
More than a maid outfit?

00:23:27.770 --> 00:23:29.200
What about a kimono?

00:23:29.200 --> 00:23:31.400
I wish I could line lots of you up on my dresser.

00:23:31.400 --> 00:23:34.020
That would just make me a wooden doll!

00:23:34.020 --> 00:23:35.980
But it'd be so cute...
